  "implementation": [
    "Relay-only policy suppresses direct host and server-reflexive candidates. Explicit UDP/TCP TURN control uses real UDP relay allocations and permissions; unsupported secure schemes refuse. No implicit public STUN service.",
    "TURN control sockets and sans-I/O clients belong to the original RTC driver, without detached relay workers. Per-peer route/control bounds apply. TURN control transport is independent of requested UDP relay transport.",
    "Owned canonical RTP and DTMF writes encapsulate exactly the original output and complete the actual wire send inside the original guarded write. No application packet survives into a later unguarded control poll, including output-capacity refusal. A cancelled/failed TCP write taints the stream so later writes refuse.",
    "Close retains the original driver handle while awaiting bounded authenticated Refresh/lifetime-zero acknowledgements. Unknown allocation/timeout or failed cleanup reports unconfirmed rather than success. Existing direct-only close remains unchanged.",
    "Still-owned relay candidates are emitted on regather; actual ICE restart/recovery qualification remains open."
  ],
